{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/192179-scion-exalted-cool","id":192179,"title":"Scion + Exalted = Cool?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-09T01:28:27-07:00","id":192179,"title":"Scion + Exalted = Cool?","content":"So, I wanted to add a few things from Exalted into Scion. Some small things, like Prayer rules, Character Creation tweaks, etc., but I'm also interested in adding some bigger stuff, like Martial Arts Forms, Sorcery Spells, Astrology, etc. So, I wanted to know, about where would Exalted Martial Arts Styles fit? Like, do you think Terrestrial Styles are on par with the Hero Cycle? Or maybe Celestial Styles are a better fit? What about Sorcery? Would the three levels fit the three Scion Cycles? I was thinking of using it to replace the Magic Purview, it just seems more interesting to me. I was also thinking of replacing Mystery or Prophecy with Astrology. I'm more interested in the Power Levels and how they stack up against one another than if I SHOULD do it or not. I know how many feel about adding Exalted to, well, anything. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the input!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T02:39:07-07:00","id":192206,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Scion's system and Exalted's may use similar rules, but they don't play very nicely together. Epic Attributes don't even work properly inside Scion, much less when you toss in Charms. You'd have a much easier time just running Exalted in a modern setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T04:07:06-07:00","id":192236,"title":"","content":"Sure, Charms I can see as being a bit of a problem, especially with Epic Attributes and the like, but what about Sorcery? I feel like the Exalted Sorcery has more...Flavor, you know? Same with Astrology. I wanted to make the 3 &quot;occult&quot; Purviews, idk, different. Or more different than the other Purviews. Looking over the Spells, I don't really see a problem at this point, but I could be missing something. Obviously, as with both systems, Sorcery can't be used with dice adders (thus no Epics/Excellencies depending on system). In regards to Astrology, again, no problem with the system as far as I see, but has anyone tried to convert it over yet? I'd like to find one more &quot;power&quot; so I can change all 3. <br /> <br /> What do you mean the Epics don't work correctly inside Scion? I ran two Scion games, both of them went from Hero to God, both lasted 2+ years, and I never had an issue as far as I remember and if there was, it wasn't so bad that I couldn't easily fix it. In fact, the only real problem I've ever had with Scion wasn't system, it was keeping players motivated after they'd reached a specific Power level (God in the case), but that's a problem in all games, from Exalted to Hunter to non-White Wolf games, such as D&amp;D to Silver Age Sentinels to...well, you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Again, my question is about Power Levels, not about whether I should mesh the games. I'm an extremely experienced ST/GM/DM/whatever, meshing the game is easy, I just wanted input on how much more powerful, say, Charms are to Purviews or Magic is to Sorcery. Thanks for the help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T04:07:40-07:00","id":192237,"title":"","content":"Actually not long ago they published an &quot;Exalted Modern&quot; setting in the book, <i>Shards of the Exalted Dream</i>. That said, a Sidereal with a car is bizarrely scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T04:25:10-07:00","id":192265,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've read and very much enjoyed Exalted Modern, but, for several reasons, I'm going with Scion for the majority of the system. I'm looking to add a few parts from Exalted into the main Scion game. Looking at the MA Charms, they seem a little bit more powerful than knacks, but in the grand scheme, as it were, not much more. I would say they'd be bought for 4 bonus points, i.e. slightly more than knacks, but slightly less than Boons/Epics. Now, understand, I don't want to use ALL the Charms, maybe not any of them to be honest, but if I WAS going to allow them, it would JUST be the MA Charms. Just something to add to the combat. Also, I wouldn't use the Terrestrial Styles at all, too underpowered. I'm going to take a look at the Sorcery now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T04:50:08-07:00","id":192271,"title":"","content":"Sorcery, it seems to me, is more powerful to start with, but then kind of gets more...limited as you hit the God Cycle. That's not bad though, totally usable. Astrology isn't really that much more powerful or less powerful than Mystery/Prophecy so there's that as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T12:37:06-07:00","id":192633,"title":"","content":"Broadly speaking, I advise against it. They are both good games, and there are some elements that could be use (mostly rules tweaks, like we use &quot;defend other&quot; for example) but in general I don't think the supernatural powers systems between the two games play well together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T15:10:01-07:00","id":192800,"title":"","content":"My default advice is not to do it. While they resemble each other on the surface, they use a different mote/legend ratio, a different success ratio, a different resistance system, and a different set of mythology. That said...<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Martial Arts / Terrestrial Sorcery = <b>Legend 2 - 4.</b><br /> Celestial Martial Arts / Celestial Sorcery = <b>Legend 5 - 7.</b><br /> Sidereal Martial Arts / Solar Sorcery = <b>Legend 8 - 10.</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T18:54:05-07:00","id":192990,"title":"","content":"Conceptually, I\u2019d be more inclined to blend the two within the context of <b>Exalted</b>, tweaking the God-Blooded to be a bit more <b>Scion</b>-like (specifically, allowing them to rival the Exalted and potentially transform themselves into gods once their Essence gets high enough). Mechanically, I\u2019d stay firmly within the bounds of <b>Exalted</b> \u2014 e.g., borrowing from 2e\u2019s Infernal Exalted for a Charm-based mechanism for apotheosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T22:31:07-07:00","id":193160,"title":"","content":"Thank you Iry, that's the kind of thing I was looking for. Thank you all for the advice, though again, I reiterate, I understand the trials and tribulations that meshing the systems bring about. I'm JUST looking for Power Comparisons. Honestly, I just wanted to see if anyone had done a Comparison before so I could be lazy. I'm a long time ST of both games, so I know the system of each inside and out, I suppose I can just do the comparison myself. I'm a little baffled as to why everyone thinks it's so hard to cram some Exalted rules into Scion. I'm not talking about (again) adding all the Charms of Exalted into Scion. I'm not talking about meshing them in a way that would have equal parts of both. I'm just adding in a FEW STYLES to spice up combat. Easily done. Sorcery, Necromancy and Astrology are all just as easy.<br /> <br /> Now, in my opinion, I would go with Essence Min. = Legend Min. when using MA Styles. It's seriously that easy. As I mentioned, they seem slightly more powerful than Knacks, but not as powerful as Epics/Boons. The Sorcery/Necromancy, as I said, is a bit more powerful at Hero, equal in Demigod and underpowered in God. Astrology is just a system that would always be useful regardless of Cycle. If anyone is interested, I can let you know how it goes, but I'm not really expecting any issues. It seems that both Exalted and Scion have a system that others are finding &quot;Impossible&quot; and &quot;Unplayable&quot;, but as I said, I've run both, for years, and have found the games both possible and playable, so I'm kind of interested in WHY people think this. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T09:05:39-07:00","id":196323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/192179-scion-exalted-cool?p=192990#post192990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conceptually, I\u2019d be more inclined to blend the two within the context of <b>Exalted</b>, tweaking the God-Blooded to be a bit more <b>Scion</b>-like... specifically, allowing them to rival the Exalted...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's mostly just a problem of mechanics; the upcoming edition suggests that the overall power curve is being flattened a bit, so that even mortals can at least threaten an Exalt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/192179-scion-exalted-cool?p=192990#post192990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and potentially transform themselves into gods once their Essence gets high enough...</div> </div> </div> </div>That already happens. God-Blooded and other half-<i>x</i> humans are capped at Essence 3, and should they reach Essence 4, it comes paired with an apotheosis of sorts.<br /> <br /> The downside is that on paper, they can't do it on their own, but that's fixed easily enough.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T13:07:18-07:00","id":197120,"title":"","content":"I run an Exalted-Scion cross over game. Actually works quite fine since house rules were needed for the Scions. Solars still outshine everyone though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T17:10:15-07:00","id":197269,"title":"","content":"I'll be the first to admit i don't have the practice with Scion of the Baron and some of the other people present, but the biggest hurdles i see in getting the two games together are the Scion's ludricous amount of sucesses even in comparison to Exalted's, let's be honest here, already inflated standards and matters of mythology (Fate in Scion is completely unlike its namesake in Exalted and closer to Raksha's notion of evolution through the development of an epic narrative, the character of Scion's underworld &amp; overworld in relation to Creation &amp; co, what Scion's Titans &amp; deities actually are, titans &amp; their avatars seeming momewhere between Unshaped &amp; 3rd Circle Demons in thematics &amp; presentation, among other stuff).<br /> <br /> Admitedly, the setting/mythology part is much less of an issue if one keeps the two worlds separate creations/realms of existence (beyond Deep Wyld/Well of Udr), but can still quite relevant.<br /> <br /> Yes, cost differences and other things exist, but purview boons and epic attribute knacks could be ported as charms with little problem in concept, if not actual mechanics.<br /> <br /> Legend and Essence while filling mostly the same function seem to have some differences in treatment and because of this and matters of scale i toyed with the following equivalence:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Legend</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Essence</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1 (unenlightened)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">1-2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1-2 (enlightened)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">3-4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2-3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">5-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3-4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">7-8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">4-5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">9-10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">5-6</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">11-12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">6-7</td> </tr> </table></div> The legend/essence pool one may or not stay the same depending on individual ST's convenience/laziness, but no, i have no particular suggestion on how to calculate such pools beside fake something and filling the blanks with mote pool enhancers like Essence Plethora.<br /> <br /> Don't know if it will be useful or useless but hope it may get your interest at least. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T05:17:56-07:00","id":197810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/192179-scion-exalted-cool?p=197269#post197269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Legend</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Essence</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1 (unenlightened)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">1-2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1-2 (enlightened)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">3-4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2-3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">5-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3-4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">7-8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">4-5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">9-10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">5-6</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">11-12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">6-7</td> </tr> </table></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa there! Legend 12 would be dramatically above Essence 6-7, unless you meant for them to represent themes and not mechanical balance. Perfects are the only thing that keeps Scions from stomping all over Exalts in early Demigod, and when a Scion hits Legend 12, not even perfects will save them anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T07:03:51-07:00","id":197886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/192179-scion-exalted-cool?p=197810#post197810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[W]hen a Scion hits Legend 12, not even perfects will save them anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoo, that's a can of worms we're opening right there.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, by Legend 12 the Scion is farting out multiple free Perfect-or-Die attacks with every action and still sits chilling outside the practical range of probability for even an Essence 10 Solar to connect a single blow without some sort of auto-hit charm.<br /> <br /> But perfect defenses are perfect defenses, and I'd say that there's no reason they wouldn't still work--part of their core principle is &quot;there is no more-perfect-than-perfect attack that supercedes this.&quot; In a 2.0 environment that fight's still going to be going on for a Very Long Time.<br /> <br /> Also, that sound you hear is the ugly grinding noise of two closely-related-but-still-different systems colliding with each other.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T11:10:08-07:00","id":198063,"title":"","content":"Something about that word &quot;God&quot; that should say <i>something</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T12:41:00-07:00","id":198128,"title":"","content":"Something about the phrase &quot;Primordial Slayers&quot; also needs to be said there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T14:23:49-07:00","id":198234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/192179-scion-exalted-cool?p=198063#post198063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something about that word &quot;God&quot; that should say <i>something</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should! But they're two games separated by a common vocabulary:<br /> <br /> A God in Scion is a mythic figure writ large, lasting through the centuries, possessed of ineffable power and wisdom. Their children are champions blessed upon the world, the making of legends which shall never be forgot.<br /> <br /> A God in Exalted is a spiritual figure who may be in charge of the Heavens, this here rice field, or that slightly bent nail over there in the wall. Their children are a bit...*more* than normal, but not by that much. Assuming a shared area of expertise, the titular Exalted will generally rapidly outgrow and dominate: They were made to wrestle with things larger than mere <i>gods</i>.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T15:53:03-07:00","id":198279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/192179-scion-exalted-cool?p=197886#post197886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, yeah, by Legend 12 the Scion is farting out multiple free Perfect-or-Die attacks with every action and still sits chilling outside the practical range of probability for even an Essence 10 Solar to connect a single blow without some sort of auto-hit charm.<br /> <br /> But perfect defenses are perfect defenses, and I'd say that there's no reason they wouldn't still work--part of their core principle is &quot;there is no more-perfect-than-perfect attack that supercedes this.&quot; In a 2.0 environment that fight's still going to be going on for a Very Long Time.<br /> <br /> Also, that sound you hear is the ugly grinding noise of two closely-related-but-still-different systems colliding with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is not that perfect defenses wouldn't work. The issue is that Avatars are scene long narrative events. The Scion player pops an Avatar, then looks at the Solar player and says <i>&quot;Alright, describe how your character dramatically resists my overwhelming power until he runs out of motes and dies.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T16:05:55-07:00","id":198297,"title":"","content":"The Totem Pole of Power has always been <b>Nobilis &gt; Scion &gt; Exalted.</b><br /> Coincidentally, Rebecca Borgstrom was an influence in all three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T16:36:58-07:00","id":198317,"title":"","content":"Well, a good thing I've never been a fan of &quot;Exalted.&quot; To me it's laughable to imagine a &quot;Solar&quot; giving Thor a beat down who likely looks at said character as an itty bitty nail needing a hammer blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T22:16:36-07:00","id":198558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/192179-scion-exalted-cool?p=198279#post198279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is not that perfect defenses wouldn't work. The issue is that Avatars are scene long narrative events. The Scion player pops an Avatar, then looks at the Solar player and says <i>&quot;Alright, describe how your character dramatically resists my overwhelming power until he runs out of motes and dies.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And the issue with that is that in a 2.0 environment--which is the paradigm about the time that Scion was being released, so let's go with that--even a starting Solar has theoretical access to the tools that can keep their head above water and perfect everything for hours with <i>terrifying efficiency</i>.<br /> <br /> I am not trying to deny that Scion's Gods are even more horrendously overpowered than the Exalted--an epic feat in and of itself--so much as make a case that even removed from their milieu, the Exalted don't just fall like so much chaff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T02:50:48-07:00","id":198760,"title":"","content":"Again, please understand, I'm not meshing the two games together. I'm going with a SCION game that adds ONE, maybe TWO, things from EXALTED. I'm VERY interested in SORCERY and how it measures up to MAGIC. That's the big one. I'm already adding in Astrology because it's just cooler than the option in Scion. The second thing I'm wanting information is how would Celestial Martial Arts measure up in Scion. The purpose in this is just to spice up the combat monkeys that Scions are.<br /> <br /> That's it. Just Sorcery and Martial Arts. Everything else is Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:58:59-07:00","id":199002,"title":"","content":"Edit: I cut up my original post because honestly, i don't care that much to defend that little table i made up or whatever. Distracts too much of the main topic, might add unnecessary fuel to a fire better quenched and the OP manifested itself to further explain what it has in mind.<br /> <br /> So, on with the boat and here goes nothing:<br /> <br /> On adding Sorcery and Martial Arts to Scion? Well, i don't really know how that would work out. What makes those things special in Exalted is their nature as &quot;uneven but common ground&quot; between the many varied types of supernatural entities tied to Creation a function of their role &quot;stuff to let characters get powers outside the themes of their type&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sorcery with its &quot;catch as catch can&quot; attitude to spells is closer to most purviews in arrangement than Scion's Magic from what i remember, the idea of effects more powerful than usual for one's Legend level that require &quot;loading time&quot; and the potential option of an &quot;auto-undo&quot; in the form of countermagic certainly has merit. Summoning &amp; banishment are cool but could probably be done just as well or better through Purviews.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile on Scion &quot;type themes&quot; is far less of a deal - if it can even be said to be one - scions and lesser immortals/titanspawn are more embryonic gods/greater titanspawn than actual different entities. The greatest &quot;distinction of nature&quot; in the setting would be titanic x divine divide that defines the main conflict of Scion - and what actually separates them in those is how much Fate influenced them or not in developing a certain &quot;more human&quot; set of virtues/culture/values and a (pantheon) specific Purview that resonates with that set of virtues. Commonalities prevail and theme more of a matter of what an individual being favors, it's the opposite of the situation that makes Sorcery and Martial Arts a sort of sub-system in Exalted.<br /> <br /> That said, they do possess a &quot;fire stolen from the gods&quot; appeal, terrain with very little coverage in Scion, that is a niche Sorcery &amp; esoteric martial arts might fit in. However, the fact mortals don't have or use Legend naturally, energy costs in Exalted in relation to energy costs in Scion among other things would serious tweaking unavoidable. Also, there are a few things already in that niche a ST could more easily work from, like mortals as low-level guides, the rules for heroic mortal companions or the artifacts of the Order of the Divine Glory (both in Scion Companion) are a few i can remember.<br /> <br /> Though on a little aside, <b>Thaumaturgy </b>with its basis on resources to sacrifice, be they expensive materials, blood, jade or magic energies harvested from relics or places of mystic significance offers just as many possibities as Sorcery with none of the hassle to adapt, as you can basically use it as is on Scion games and little to no work to port over. Might cook up some extra rituals with a virtue requirement for color, or some rule to lower ritual costs when focusing an appropriate virtue in the roll or &quot;sacrificing&quot; a virtue-ressonant action/stunt for legend, but not much beyond that.<br /> <br /> Another thing that crossed my mind is - Magic, from what i can remember of the books, IS Scion's equivalent of fate-weaving, so sidereal astrology and charms might be a much better comparison/foil than Sorcery, that is about shaping and conjuring things, beings and forces up from the fabric of reality. But either way, reworking Fate means reworking Sorcery as a whole, because they're inextricably connected afaik.<br /> <br /> Well, longish post, but those are my thoughts on the objectives you brought up, blindST - my initial impression is that overall there's not much call for either Sorcery or esoteric MA in Scion (specially the latter, as the setting lacks the strong wuxia influence/imagery that defines it) and while there is at least one good niche in &quot;fire stolen from the gods&quot; theme, resonant but little explored in the game, there are also quicker and cleaner alternatives to mine in Scion (guides &amp; aforementioned stuff in the Companion) and Exalted (Thaumaturgy) both for that and if you do, they can rock mightly. Hope these ingredients help with cooking some this game you are brewing.<br /> <br /> Would really like to hear of what you have to say on this, maybe give it a little try myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-16-2014, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}